    "body": "Uniform rational-height choices can exclude leaf-dependent HHG certificates before lattice reduction, and degree0/1 modulus shifts can leave short rows inside the original integer-lift ideal. This PR adds generic support tests and a different proposed candidate: concentrate the total chart-height shrink on a few coordinates and match a sparse modulus-monomial menu to the constraint support. Eligibility is distinct from a positive determinant margin or useful independent equations. [pcc:unverified]\n\nThe final package includes universal shift-pool and subcritical chart bounds, ordinary-ideal filtration and exact projective witnesses, an unexecuted capped saturation/recovery prototype, and the new anisotropic-height/support analysis. The new menu/profile successor is specified and has not been implemented in the earlier frozen scalar-height/degree0/1 prototype. Centered modular lifts are not identified silently with the exact characteristic-zero S3 ideal. The complete classical subexponential prime-field ECDLP algorithm remains unestablished. [pcc:unverified]\n\nLocal validation: canonical all-tracked Lean audit293/0/0 exits0. The newest component contributes fifteen generic laws and eight actual semantic declarations, with standard named axiom dependencies; earlier components contribute twenty-two generic laws. Prior Python/Sage source has seven Python/seven JSON files parsed and nine noncryptographic development controls passing, with no scientific Sage/curve/LLL, paid or qualification run. All four final anisotropic-report pages were inspected. Positive determinant gain, whole-chain independence, charged finite-root cost and useful random-target yield remain open. [pcc:unverified]\n\nScoped claims PCC-20261116-8ad24e, PCC-20261116-c2eaec, PCC-20261116-2c3e0c and PCC-20261116-58f919 remain unverified. All158 pinned subjects match; all137 previous pins and the published twelve-row ledger remain exact, with the new thirteen-row chain verified. Raw compiler failures and warning whitespace are retained; owned source/prose whitespace checks pass. No independent signed verdict or evaluated identity certificate. Numerical trial admission still needs the existing live cost/reservation record, source-bound runtime and actual caller/capacity/custody checks. [pcc:unverified]\n\nReports: docs/universal-shift-pool-20261116.md; docs/balanced-height-filtration-20261116.md; docs/saturated-selector-prototype-20261116.md; docs/anisotropic-height-budget-20261116.md. [pcc:unverified]\n",
